                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This guide applies when you have:<br />
- Completed TikTok Shop store setup and product listing<br />
- Prepared to launch ad campaigns for new products<br />
- Aimed to accumulate initial data and establish performance benchmarks during the cold start phase (typically the first 14 days after launch)</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>The core cold start goal is not ROI, but helping TikTok's algorithm identify your target audience characteristics. The richness of your asset pool directly impacts cold start success rate.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Define Your Asset Type Mix</h2>
<p>For the cold start phase, prepare the following 4 asset categories simultaneously:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Asset Type</th>
<th>Recommended Quantity</th>
<th>Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Primary videos (15-60s)</td>
<td>4-6 pieces</td>
<td>Core conversion assets for scaling</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Quick hook videos (3-7s)</td>
<td>8-10 pieces</td>
<td>Test fast engagement capability</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Carousel images (3-5 slides)</td>
<td>3-5 sets</td>
<td>Supplement placements, cover showcase scenarios</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>UGC-style testimonial (20-30s)</td>
<td>3-4 pieces</td>
<td>Simulate real user experience, build trust</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Key principle</strong>: Don't concentrate all budgets on one asset format. Recommend 60% budget to primary videos, 20% to quick hook videos, and 20% to carousels. Adjust based on performance data.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Plan Asset Theme Directions</h2>
<p>Before filming, extract 3-5 core narrative angles based on product selling points. Avoid producing randomly.</p>
<h3>Common Narrative Direction Checklist</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Pain point resonance</strong>: Show users' daily frustrations first, then introduce the product solution</li>
<li><strong>Before/after comparison</strong>: Highlight actual product results</li>
<li><strong>Scene integration</strong>: Naturally embed products into target users' frequent usage scenarios</li>
<li><strong>Review endorsement</strong>: Use KOC-style narration to explain ingredients, features, and experience</li>
<li><strong>Limited promotion</strong>: Create urgency with TikTok Shop exclusive offers</li>
</ol>
<p>For each narrative direction, produce at least 2 assets to prevent total campaign failure if a single direction underperforms.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Upload Assets and Group Management</h2>
<p>After preparing assets, follow these rules when uploading to TikTok Ads Manager:</p>
<h3>Naming Convention</h3>
<pre><code>[Product Line]-[Asset Type]-[Narrative Direction]-[Version]

Example: skincare-serum-painpoint-v1
         skincare-serum-compare-v2
</code></pre>
<h3>Upload Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Video resolution ≥ 720p, recommended 1080×1920 (vertical)</li>
<li>[ ] File size under 500MB</li>
<li>[ ] Audio has no copyright risk (use TikTok commercial music library)</li>
<li>[ ] Cover image clear, text readable (avoid large text on small images)</li>
<li>[ ] All assets tagged appropriately (e.g., #newproduct #unboxing #review)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Execute Cold Start Testing</h2>
<h3>Testing Phase Timeline</h3>
<p><strong>Day 1-3: Rapid Screening</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Allocate $50-100 budget per asset group</li>
<li>Use broad interest targeting, observe organic traffic performance</li>
<li>Screening metrics: 3-second completion rate &gt; 40%, CVR &gt; 1.5%</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Day 4-7: Data Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Pause bottom-performing assets (CTR &lt; 0.5%)</li>
<li>Concentrate budget on Top 3 assets</li>
<li>Switch to Add to Cart (ATC) optimization goal</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Day 8-14: Stable Scaling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Keep assets with CPM &lt; $15 running continuously</li>
<li>Start testing asset iteration directions (change first 3 seconds, music, subtitles)</li>
<li>Prepare new batch of assets for handoff to prevent creative fatigue</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Common Pitfalls to Avoid</h2>
<p><strong>Pitfall 1: Severe Asset Homogenization</strong></p>
<p>Multiple assets under the same narrative direction with nearly identical opening shots, music, and copy will cause TikTok's system to flag them as duplicate assets, lowering eCPM. Ensure each direction has at least one "completely different" version.</p>
<p><strong>Pitfall 2: Ignoring TikTok's Native Feel</strong></p>
<p>Overly polished product videos often underperform on TikTok. During cold start, try "casual recording" styles, subtitle overlays, and fast editing rhythms to match platform aesthetics.</p>
<p><strong>Pitfall 3: Over-dispersed Budget Allocation</strong></p>
<p>Common beginner mistake: distributing small budgets to every asset, resulting in no single asset accumulating enough data for algorithm learning. For the first round, concentrate budget on only 2-3 main assets for focused testing.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Ongoing Asset Iteration Rhythm</h2>
<p>After cold start completion, maintain a 20% bi-weekly asset pool refresh rate:</p>
<ul>
<li>Keep stable performing legacy assets (continue scaling)</li>
<li>Remove low-efficiency assets with CTR below 0.3%</li>
<li>Add new direction test assets</li>
</ul>
<p>This maintains account vitality while preventing data fluctuation from frequent changes.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Execution Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Confirm SKU count for this cold start cycle</li>
<li>[ ] Plan asset quantities by type (refer to Step 1 table)</li>
<li>[ ] Extract 3-5 narrative directions (refer to Step 2 checklist)</li>
<li>[ ] Complete asset filming/production</li>
<li>[ ] Upload to Ads Manager with proper naming convention</li>
<li>[ ] Launch Day 1-3 rapid testing</li>
<li>[ ] Execute asset screening on Day 4</li>
<li>[ ] Enter stable scaling phase on Day 8</li>
</ul>
